.TH "fbcli" "" "" ""
.SH "نام (NAME)"
fbcli \- Emit events to feedbackd
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
.nf
\fBfbcli\fP [OPTIONS...]
.fi
.sp
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
.sp
\fBfbcli\fP can be used to submit events to \fBfeedbackd\fP to trigger
audio, visual or haptic feedback.
.SS OPTIONS
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \fB\-h\fP, \fB\-\-help\fP
print help and exit
.TP
.B \fB\-E=EVENT\fP, \fB\-\-event=EVENT\fP
Submit the given event to \fBfeedbackd\fP\&. Valid events are listes in
the event naming spec at
\%<https://\:gitlab\:.freedesktop\:.org/\:agx/\:feedbackd/\:-/\:blob/\:main/\:doc/\:Event-naming-spec-0\:.0\:.0\:.md>
.TP
.B \fB\-I\fP, \fB\-\-important\fP
Whether to set the important hint
.TP
.B \fB\-t=TIMEOUT\fP, \fB\-\-timeout=TIMEOUT\fP
The timeout in seconds after which feedback for the given event should
be stopped.
.TP
.B \fB\-P=PROFILE\fP, \fB\-\-profile=PROFILE\fP
The feedback profile (\fBfull\fP, \fBquiet\fP, \fBsilent\fP)
to use for the given event. If no event is specified then the global
feedback profile is changed.
.TP
.B \fB\-w=TIMEOUT\fP, \fB\-\-watch=TIMEOUT\fP
Maximum timeout to wait for the feedback for the given event to end and
\fBfbcli\fP to exit.
.TP
.B \fB\-A=APP_ID\fP, \fB\-\-app\-id=APP_ID\fP
Override the used application id
.TP
.B \fB\-S=SOUND_FILE\fP, \fB\-\-sound\-file=SOUND_FILE\fP
Override the sound effect used with the given file. This only has an
effect when a sound event would be triggered by this event at the
current level.
.UNINDENT
.SS See also
.sp
\fBfeedbackd(8)\fP \fBfbd\-theme\-validate(1)\fP \fBfeedback\-themes(5)\fP
